{"id":"mahabharata-13-041","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":41,"title":"एकचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 41 · Vipula guards Ruchi","summary":{"en":"Indra, in a form of divine beauty, comes to the hermitage when he sees his chance, and Vipula, by the power of yoga, enters his guru's wife's body and holds her still. Indra, abashed, sees her free of any stir, and flees in fear of the sage's curse.","kn":"ಅವಕಾಶ ಕಂಡ ಇಂದ್ರ ದಿವ್ಯ ಸೌಂದರ್ಯ ರೂಪದಲ್ಲಿ ಆಶ್ರಮಕ್ಕೆ ಬರುತ್ತಾನೆ; ವಿಪುಲ ಯೋಗಬಲದಿಂದ ಗುರುಪತ್ನಿಯ ದೇಹ ಪ್ರವೇಶಿಸಿ ಅವಳನ್ನು ಸ್ತಬ್ಧಗೊಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ನಾಚಿದ ಇಂದ್ರ ಅವಳು ವಿಕಾರರಹಿತಳಾಗಿರುವುದನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಋಷಿಯ ಶಾಪದ ಭಯದಿಂದ ಓಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अवसर देखकर इन्द्र दिव्य सुन्दर रूप में आश्रम आते हैं, और विपुल योगबल से गुरुपत्नी के शरीर में प्रवेश कर उसे स्थिर कर देता है। लज्जित इन्द्र उसे विकाररहित देखकर ऋषि के शाप के भय से भाग जाते हैं।","te":"అవకాశం చూసిన ఇంద్రుడు దివ్య సౌందర్య రూపంలో ఆశ్రమానికి వస్తాడు; విపులుడు యోగబలంతో గురుపత్ని శరీరంలో ప్రవేశించి ఆమెను నిశ్చలంగా ఉంచుతాడు. సిగ్గుపడిన ఇంద్రుడు ఆమె వికారం లేకుండా ఉండటం చూసి ఋషి శాపం భయంతో పారిపోతాడు.","ta":"வாய்ப்பைக் கண்ட இந்திரன் தெய்வ அழகு வடிவில் ஆசிரமம் வர, விபுலன் யோக வலிமையால் குருபத்தினியின் உடலில் புகுந்து அவளை அசையாமல் நிறுத்துகிறான். நாணிய இந்திரன் அவள் மாற்றமின்றி இருப்பதைக் கண்டு முனிவரின் சாபத்துக்கு அஞ்சி ஓடுகிறான்.","ml":"അവസരം കാണുമ്പോൾ ദിവ്യസൗന്ദര്യമുള്ള രൂപത്തിൽ ഇന്ദ്രൻ ആശ്രമത്തിലെത്തുന്നു; യോഗശക്തിയാൽ വിപുലൻ ഗുരുപത്നിയുടെ ശരീരത്തിൽ പ്രവേശിച്ച് അവളെ അനങ്ങാതെ നിർത്തുന്നു. ഒരു ചലനവുമില്ലാതെ അവളെ കാണുന്ന ഇന്ദ്രൻ ലജ്ജിതനാകുന്നു, മുനിയുടെ ശാപത്തെ ഭയന്ന് ഓടിപ്പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.41; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः कदाचिद्देवेन्द्रो दिव्यरूपवपुर्धरः ।\nइदमन्तरमित्येवं ततोऽभ्यागादथाश्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one day, thinking This is the opportunity, Indra, lord of the gods, took on a divine form and came to the hermitage."}},{"n":2,"text":"रूपमप्रतिमं कृत्वा लोभनीयं जनाधिप ।\nदर्शनीयतमो भूत्वा प्रविवेश तमाश्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Making himself a form beyond compare and desirable, lord of the people, he became the most beautiful of sights and entered that hermitage."}},{"n":3,"text":"स ददर्श तमासीनं विपुलस्य कलेवरम् ।\nनिश्चेष्टं स्तब्धनयनं यथालेख्यगतं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw Vipula's body sitting there motionless, with fixed eyes, as if it were a painting."}},{"n":4,"text":"रुचिं च रुचिरापाङ्गीं पीनश्रोणिपयोधराम् ।\nपद्मपत्रविशालाक्षीं संपूर्णेन्दुनिभाननाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He also saw Ruchi, with lovely eye-corners, full hips and breasts, wide eyes like lotus petals, and a face like the full moon."}},{"n":5,"text":"सा तमालोक्य सहसा प्रत्युत्थातुमियेष ह ।\nरूपेण विस्मिता कोऽसीत्यथ वक्तुमिहेच्छती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him, she suddenly wished to rise, amazed at his looks, and wanting to ask who he was."}},{"n":6,"text":"उत्थातुकामापि सती व्यतिष्ठद्विपुलेन सा ।\nनिगृहीता मनुष्येन्द्र न शशाक विचेष्टितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though she wished to rise, she remained where she was, held down by Vipula, lord of men, and could not move."}},{"n":7,"text":"तामाबभाषे देवेन्द्रः साम्ना परमवल्गुना ।\nत्वदर्थमागतं विद्धि देवेन्द्रं मां शुचिस्मिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord of the gods addressed her in very charming and gentle words: Know that I, Indra, have come for you, radiantly smiling one."}},{"n":8,"text":"क्लिश्यमानमनङ्गेन त्वत्संकल्पोद्भवेन वै ।\nतत्पर्याप्नुहि मां सुभ्रु पुरा कालोऽतिवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am tormented by love that arose from my thought of you. Give me fulfillment, fair-browed one, before the time passes."}},{"n":9,"text":"तमेवंवादिनं शक्रं शुश्राव विपुलो मुनिः ।\nगुरुपत्न्याः शरीरस्थो ददर्श च सुराधिपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage Vipula heard Indra speaking so, and, abiding in his teacher's wife's body, he saw the lord of the gods."}},{"n":10,"text":"न शशाक च सा राजन्प्रत्युत्थातुमनिन्दिता ।\nवक्तुं च नाशकद्राजन्विष्टब्धा विपुलेन सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blameless woman could neither rise nor speak, king, being held rigid by Vipula."}},{"n":11,"text":"आकारं गुरुपत्न्यास्तु विज्ञाय स भृगूद्वहः ।\nनिजग्राह महातेजा योगेन बलवत्प्रभो ।\nबबन्ध योगबन्धैश्च तस्याः सर्वेन्द्रियाणि सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Perceiving the state of his teacher's wife, the mighty descendant of Bhrigu, lord, controlled her forcefully by yoga, and bound all her senses with bonds of yoga."}},{"n":12,"text":"तां निर्विकारां दृष्ट्वा तु पुनरेव शचीपतिः ।\nउवाच व्रीडितो राजंस्तां योगबलमोहिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing her unmoved, the lord of Shachi, ashamed, spoke again to her, king, who was dazed by the power of yoga."}},{"n":13,"text":"एह्येहीति ततः सा तं प्रतिवक्तुमियेष च ।\nस तां वाचं गुरोः पत्न्या विपुलः पर्यवर्तयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Come, come! she then wished to reply to him, but Vipula turned that speech of his teacher's wife around."}},{"n":14,"text":"भोः किमागमने कृत्यमिति तस्याश्च निःसृता ।\nवक्त्राच्छशाङ्कप्रतिमाद्वाणी संस्कारभूषिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"There came from her moon-like face, refined and polished, the words: Sir, what business brings you here?"}},{"n":15,"text":"व्रीडिता सा तु तद्वाक्यमुक्त्वा परवशा तदा ।\nपुरंदरश्च संत्रस्तो बभूव विमनास्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashamed, having said those words, she was then not her own mistress, and Indra grew alarmed and troubled in mind."}},{"n":16,"text":"स तद्वैकृतमालक्ष्य देवराजो विशां पते ।\nअवैक्षत सहस्राक्षस्तदा दिव्येन चक्षुषा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Noticing her change, the thousand-eyed king of the gods, lord of the people, then looked with his divine eye."}},{"n":17,"text":"ददर्श च मुनिं तस्याः शरीरान्तरगोचरम् ।\nप्रतिबिम्बमिवादर्शे गुरुपत्न्याः शरीरगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw the sage moving inside her body, like a reflection in a mirror, within his teacher's wife's body."}},{"n":18,"text":"स तं घोरेण तपसा युक्तं दृष्ट्वा पुरंदरः ।\nप्रावेपत सुसंत्रस्तः शापभीतस्तदा विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him endowed with terrible austerity, Indra trembled, greatly frightened and afraid of a curse, lord."}},{"n":19,"text":"विमुच्य गुरुपत्नीं तु विपुलः सुमहातपाः ।\nस्वं कलेवरमाविश्य शक्रं भीतमथाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vipula, the great ascetic, released his teacher's wife, re-entered his own body, and said to the frightened Indra:"}},{"n":20,"text":"अजितेन्द्रिय पापात्मन्कामात्मक पुरंदर ।\nन चिरं पूजयिष्यन्ति देवास्त्वां मानुषास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra, of unmastered senses and sinful mind, ruled by desire, gods and men will not honor you for long."}},{"n":21,"text":"किं नु तद्विस्मृतं शक्र न तन्मनसि ते स्थितम् ।\nगौतमेनासि यन्मुक्तो भगाङ्कपरिचिह्नितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Have you forgotten, Indra? Does it not stay in your mind how Gautama released you, marked with the signs of a thousand wombs?"}},{"n":22,"text":"जाने त्वां बालिशमतिमकृतात्मानमस्थिरम् ।\nमयेयं रक्ष्यते मूढ गच्छ पाप यथागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know you for childish-minded, unrefined and unsteady. She is guarded by me, fool. Go as you came, sinner."}},{"n":23,"text":"नाहं त्वामद्य मूढात्मन्दहेयं हि स्वतेजसा ।\nकृपायमाणस्तु न ते दग्धुमिच्छामि वासव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Foolish one, I will not burn you today with my own fire. Out of pity, Indra, I do not want to burn you."}},{"n":24,"text":"स च घोरतपा धीमान्गुरुर्मे पापचेतसम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा त्वां निर्दहेदद्य क्रोधदीप्तेन चक्षुषा ॥","meaning":{"en":"My wise teacher of dread austerity, seeing you of sinful heart, would burn you today with eyes blazing with anger."}},{"n":25,"text":"नैवं तु शक्र कर्तव्यं पुनर्मान्याश्च ते द्विजाः ।\nमा गमः ससुतामात्योऽत्ययं ब्रह्मबलार्दितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra, you must not do this again, and brahmins must be respected by you. Do not go to ruin with your sons and ministers, oppressed by the power of Brahman."}},{"n":26,"text":"अमरोऽस्मीति यद्बुद्धिमेतामास्थाय वर्तसे ।\nमावमंस्था न तपसामसाध्यं नाम किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"You live with the thought that you are immortal. Do not despise austerities, for nothing is unattainable by them."}},{"n":27,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा वचनं शक्रो विपुलस्य महात्मनः ।\nअकिंचिदुक्त्वा व्रीडितस्तत्रैवान्तरधीयत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the words of the great-souled Vipula, Indra said nothing, ashamed, and vanished on the spot."}},{"n":28,"text":"मुहूर्तयाते शक्रे तु देवशर्मा महातपाः ।\nकृत्वा यज्ञं यथाकाममाजगाम स्वमाश्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A moment after Indra had gone, the great ascetic Devasharma, having performed the sacrifice as he wished, came back to his hermitage."}},{"n":29,"text":"आगतेऽथ गुरौ राजन्विपुलः प्रियकर्मकृत् ।\nरक्षितां गुरवे भार्यां न्यवेदयदनिन्दिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the teacher returned, king, Vipula, who delighted in doing him good, reported that his blameless wife had been guarded for him."}},{"n":30,"text":"अभिवाद्य च शान्तात्मा स गुरुं गुरुवत्सलः ।\nविपुलः पर्युपातिष्ठद्यथापूर्वमशङ्कितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having saluted him, the serene Vipula, devoted to his teacher, waited upon him as before, without apprehension."}},{"n":31,"text":"विश्रान्ताय ततस्तस्मै सहासीनाय भार्यया ।\nनिवेदयामास तदा विपुलः शक्रकर्म तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the teacher had rested and was sitting with his wife, Vipula then told him of Indra's deed."}},{"n":32,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा स मुनिस्तुष्टो विपुलस्य प्रतापवान् ।\nबभूव शीलवृत्ताभ्यां तपसा नियमेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing it, the mighty sage was pleased with Vipula, for his conduct, character, austerity and discipline."}},{"n":33,"text":"विपुलस्य गुरौ वृत्तिं भक्तिमात्मनि च प्रभुः ।\nधर्मे च स्थिरतां दृष्ट्वा साधु साध्वित्युवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Vipula's service to his teacher, his devotion to himself, and his steadiness in dharma, the master said: Well done, well done."}},{"n":34,"text":"प्रतिनन्द्य च धर्मात्मा शिष्यं धर्मपरायणम् ।\nवरेण च्छन्दयामास स तस्माद्गुरुवत्सलः ।\nअनुज्ञातश्च गुरुणा चचारानुत्तमं तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The righteous teacher congratulated his pupil, who was devoted to dharma, and offered him a boon of his choice. With his teacher's leave, devoted to him, Vipula practiced supreme austerity."}},{"n":35,"text":"तथैव देवशर्मापि सभार्यः स महातपाः ।\nनिर्भयो बलवृत्रघ्नाच्चचार विजने वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise Devasharma, the great ascetic, with his wife, lived fearlessly in a solitary forest, safe from the slayer of Bala and Vritra."}}]}]}